  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nInitial closed low off the Pac NW coast will open up and kick inland \nlate Tue/Wed. This will bring a bump in precipitation chances, \nmostly across e-central Oregon and the w-central Idaho mtns. Warm \nand breezy conditions will precede this feature on Tuesday with \ntemperatures 5-10 degrees above normal and gusts across open terrain \napproaching 30 mph. \n\nRemainder of the forecast period will be dominated by a deep closed \nlow that takes position along the OR/WA coast. There is consensus \nbetween deterministic solutions and ensemble mean to keep the closed \nlow center to our west through Saturday. This puts our region under \nsouthwest flow as the low slowly fills. Looking at the details there \nare distinct forecast differences in size of the low and position it \ntakes. Would put higher confidence on cooler/wetter conditions \nacross SE Oregon zones for Thu-Sat. The ensemble mean paints 25-50% \nchance of precipitation during this period with a focus on Wed/Thur \nfor the higher probabilities. For southwest Idaho zones, have higher \nconfidence in cooler temps than seeing wetter conditions due to \nlikelihood of a dry slot setting up between precipitation circling \nthe low center and monsoon moisture further to our east. The w-\ncentral mtns would be most favored for precipitation Wed/Thur. \nBreezy/gusty winds can be expected through the period, especially \nduring the afternoon/evening. Typically favorable spots for the \nstrongest winds in this pattern are SE Oregon and higher terrain \nsouth of the Snake Plain. Starting Thursday temperatures will run \nabout 10 degrees below normal (mid-upper 70s in Snake Plain).",
